<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="h-100" data-theme="light">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>Unpublished Geocaches</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Fetch your unpublished Geocaches and create a GPX with them.">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:wght@600;700&family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <script>
        (function () {
            var theme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
            if (!theme) {
                theme = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
            }
            document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);
        })();
    </script>
    {% block javascripts %}
        {% block importmap %}{{ importmap('app') }}{% endblock %}
    {% endblock %}
</head>
<body class="d-flex flex-column h-100">

    <header>
        <nav class="navbar">
            <div class="container">
                <span class="navbar-brand-name">
                    <span class="text-orange">◎</span> Unpublished Geocaches
                </span>
                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3">
                    <div class="theme-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Color theme">
                        <button type="button" data-set-theme="light" title="Light theme" aria-label="Light theme"><i class="bi bi-sun-fill"></i></button>
                        <button type="button" data-set-theme="dark" title="Dark theme" aria-label="Dark theme"><i class="bi bi-moon-fill"></i></button>
                    </div>
                    {% if app.user is empty %}
                        <a href="{{ path('app_login') }}" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm px-4">Sign in</a>
                    {% else %}
                        <div class="hello-user">
                            <img src="{{ app.user.avatarUrl }}" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" class="rounded-circle" alt="{{ app.user.username }}'s avatar">
                            <span>{{ app.user.username }}</span>
                        </div>
                        <a href="{{ path('app_logout') }}" class="text-muted small text-decoration-none border-start ps-3" style="border-color: var(--divider) !important;" title="Sign out">Sign out</a>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </div>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="flex-shrink-0">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                {% if exception is defined %}
                    <div class="col-12">
                        <div class="alert alert-danger mt-4" role="alert">
                            <strong>{{ exception.type }}:</strong> {{ exception.message }} (Code: {{ exception.code }})
                        </div>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
                {% block main %}{% endblock %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer mt-auto py-4">
        <div class="container">
            <ul class="mb-0">
                <li><i class="bi bi-question-circle"></i> <a href="#help" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#help">About</a></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-github"></i> <a href="https://github.com/Surfoo/unpublished-geocaches">GitHub</a></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <div id="help" class="modal fade" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h4 class="modal-title">About</h4>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p>The "Unpublished Geocaches" app allows you to create GPX files from your unpublished geocaches, to prepare an event for example. If your future geocaches are already locked by a reviewer, you need to search them manually with the field on the top of the page.</p>

                    <h5>Attribution</h5>
                    <p>
                        <span style="float: right; padding: 0 0 0 12px;">
                            <a href="https://www.geocaching.com"><img src="{{ asset('live.png') }}" alt="Geocaching API"></a>
                        </span>
                        Powered by the Geocaching API. Made possible through the support of Geocaching Premium Memberships, the API program gives third-party developers the opportunity to work with Geocaching HQ on a full suite of integrated products and services for the community. API developer applications are designed to work with the core services of geocaching.com and provide additional features to the geocaching community.
                    </p>

                    <h5>Privacy Policy</h5>
                    <p>
                        "Unpublished Geocaches" collects some information about the connected user in order to keep them connected with a session cookie.<br>
                        "Unpublished Geocaches" collects only your unpublished geocaches.<br>
                        "Unpublished Geocaches" does not share any of your personal data with third parties.<br>
                        Your created GPX files are deleted after 24 hours. You can exercise your data rights by sending the name of the GPX file to delete by email (see below).
                    </p>

                    <h5>Contact</h5>
                    <p>For questions, bugs, or suggestions: <strong>surfooo at gmail dot com</strong></p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {% block body_scripts %}{% endblock %}

</body>
</html>
